Security review, stage 3: in QAUDION_TRANSPORT_STRICT builds the DTLS 1.3
minimum and the AES-256-only cipher configuration are now fixed at compile
time (#if QAUDION_TRANSPORT_STRICT) instead of depending only on the
out-of-line qaudion::TransportLevel() returning 3. The relaxed upstream
cipher list ("...:!AESGCM+AES256:...") is therefore compiled only into the
switchable (LiveKit) variant; before, it was present in every plain binary
too, so the binary gate G2 ("plain build must not contain
'!AESGCM+AES256'") would have failed every plain build.

